<title>HONG KONG: Chai Wan bid sets record for HK land auctions.</title>
<headline>Chai Wan bid sets record for HK land auctions.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The HK$11.82 billion bid that won the Chai Wan site at Tuesday's government land auction was the highest ever, auctioneer Herbert Leung said.</p>
<p>But Leung, a government land agent, noted that the bid did not represent the highest accomodation value since the 25,592 square metre site was very large.</p>
<p>Chief estate officer Paul Tam said the government had sold 10 plots of land totalling 63,154 square metres in five auctions during the fiscal year ending March 31.</p>
<p>The 10 plots attracted a total of HK$15.46 billion, he said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
